### Demographics: the census as a tab of the Population panel and a subtab of the state panel
### (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-demographics-design.md §10; plan Tasks 13-14; issue #1029, which modelled the
### panel on Banking's).
###
### A type library, one type per section (gui_style_guide.md rule 9). gui/te_demographics_layout.gui sets their order
### for both hosts: gui/pops_overview.gui instances its te_demog_tab_sections in the Population panel's fifth tab
### (te_demog), gui/states_panel.gui its te_state_demog_content as the state panel's fourth Population subtab. The
### country's sections, in that order:
###   te_demog_overview         always shown: the census year and eight icon cells, two to a row (rule 4): natural
###                             change, net migration, life expectancy, the leading cause of death, fertility, median
###                             age, working age and the Gini, each with a figure beneath and most with a trend arrow
###   te_demog_sec_causes       open: last year's deaths per 1,000, a pie of them by cause with its legend, Health
###                             Care Access (issue #1029)
###   te_demog_sec_pyramid      open: the sex balance, then 18 five-year bands, men left, women right, with the outline
###                             twenty years ahead
###   te_demog_sec_work         open: Work and Retirement (phase 2 step 2): the workforce, old age from, the pension age
###                             and its five buttons, the pensioners, the pension bill, health need, Fighting-Age Men
###                             (te_demog_fam_row) and, while a state has a youth bulge, Youth
###   te_demog_sec_longevity    open, once the late figures exist: Living to 100, biological age, longevity care and the
###                             longevity gap (phase 3)
###   te_demog_sec_family       open: the Family & Reproductive Policy law and its measures, a row and a button each;
###                             the measures other laws allow, dimmed (phase 2 step 3a)
###   te_demog_sec_history      open: eight charts by census year, with pips for war, famine and demographic events
###   te_demog_sec_wealth       open: the Gini beside the strata's incomes, Wealth Concentration as a bar heading for
###                             its target, the target's six terms, the most and least concentrated states
###   te_demog_sec_places       open: urban share, primacy, the effective number of cities, the pattern, the three
###                             largest cities
###   te_demog_sec_states       open: the ten largest states, a row each that opens the state, and Show All for the 40
###   te_demog_sec_how          collapsed: How Demographics Works
### The state's, from the same building blocks with the state's own figures (State.MakeScope.Var(...), never the
### player's): te_state_demog_overview, _causes, _pyramid (with the urban share), _work, _longevity, _wealth and _how.
### The state's Wealth shows its target's six terms: three its own, the law, tax and economic ones its owner's
### (State.GetOwner.MakeScope).
### A state has no outline, no history and no Family Policy.
###
### TYPE SIZES (rule 3; the owner's pass of 2026-10-17 on Banking): rows, values, buttons, column heads and notes in
### te_demog_fontsize_row (17), subheadings and chart titles in te_demog_fontsize_heading (20), the overview's cells in
### te_demog_fontsize_overview (16, the tooltip face). The charts' legends and axis labels keep vanilla's medium, as
### Banking's do. test_demographics_layout's WidthTest reads each cell's font and width from the markup and holds the
### longest text a cell can show to it.
###
### EDITING RULES
### * No Scope in GUI can ask whether a variable exists, and reading a missing one logs every frame (gui_modding_guide.md
###   gotchas #14 and #23). Every figure is read under a gate that asks script: the census
###   (te_pops_demog_tab_unlock_sgui's IsValid, te_dg_census_year), a stepped census for births, deaths and migration
###   (te_demog_stepped_sgui), deaths by cause (te_demog_dc_ready_sgui), Wealth Concentration's national figures
###   (te_demog_wealth_ready_sgui), the country's Gini (te_demog_gini_ready_sgui: written under a narrower condition
###   than the national figures, so it has its own gate), the outline (te_demog_outline_ready_sgui) and the capital's
###   census (te_demog_capital_census_sgui), and the state's own (te_demog_state_*_sgui, GuiScope.SetRoot(
###   State.MakeScope ).End); common/scripted_guis/te_demog_sguis.txt. A loc key that reads a gated figure is picked by
###   SelectLocalization on the gate, so the branch not taken is never rendered.
### * Country figures read GetPlayer.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_x').GetValue; a state row's, State.MakeScope.Var(...). Never
###   SCOPE.sCountry(...), which printed wrong values in the 2026-10-08 probe (scripting_best_practices.md).
### * A trend arrow tests a te_demog_trend_* code (te_demog_display_values.txt) for identity (gotcha #23): 1 rose, -1
###   fell, 0 level, 2 none.
### * A tooltip inside a datamodel row reads only that row's State (gotcha #24); a history bar's, only its
###   ScriptContainer.
### * Collapse flags say their default: *_closed sections start open, *_open ones collapsed (rule 7;
###   test_demographics_layout's FlagTest).
### * @panel_width constants are file-scoped in vanilla, so the sizes here are literals: 520 sections, a 480 column
###   inside a 20 px margin (rule 8).

### The panel's type sizes. Templates are global, so te_demographics_layout.gui reads these too.
template te_demog_fontsize_row {
	fontsize = 17
}

template te_demog_fontsize_heading {
	fontsize = 20
}

template te_demog_fontsize_overview {
	fontsize = 16
	using = tooltip_font
}

types te_demographics_widgets
{
	### ======================================================================
	### BUILDING BLOCKS (Grand Monuments' shapes, grand_monuments_widget.gui)
	### ======================================================================

	type te_demog_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		margin = { 20 8 }
		spacing = 3

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.5
		}
	}

	type te_demog_section_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			parentanchor = hcenter
			size = { 520 38 }
		}
	}

	### A heading inside a section's panel, over one group of its lines, with a
	### faint rule under it.
	type te_demog_subheader = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "subheader_margin" {
			margin_top = 10
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_heading
			default_format = "#title"
			block "subheader_text" {}
		}
		divider_clean = {
			blockoverride "size" {
				size = { 480 2 }
			}
		}
	}

	### Explanatory text under a heading in How Demographics Works.
	type te_demog_note = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = te_demog_fontsize_row
		default_format = "#lore"
	}

	### A live line of text across the panel.
	type te_demog_text = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = te_demog_fontsize_row
	}

	### A figure: its label (hover the row for what it means and last year's
	### figure), its value and a trend arrow. Fixed cells, 240 + 200 + 24 and
	### two 8 px gaps = 480, so a long label or value cannot widen the row:
	### "Wealth Concentration" is 20 characters, about 190 units in the medium
	### font; "100 men per 100 women", 21, about 200.
	type te_demog_figure_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 8

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 250 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 250 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 190 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 190 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			multiline = yes
			block "row_value" {}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 24 22 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			block "row_trend" {}
		}
	}

	### Trend arrows. The instance sets each icon's `visible` from a
	### te_demog_trend_* code. Three flavours, by whether the direction is good
	### for the player (gui_style_guide.md rule 5: green good, red bad,
	### whatever the direction):
	###   te_demog_trend_good_up    life expectancy: rising green, falling orange
	###   te_demog_trend_good_down  the dependency ratio: vanilla's arrows turned
	###                             over (mirror = vertical), so a rise is an
	###                             orange arrow pointing up
	###   te_demog_trend_neutral    a figure whose direction is neither good nor
	###                             bad in itself (median age, children per
	###                             woman, sex balance, urban share): a bronze
	###                             chevron, the politics summary's arrow, so the
	###                             colour claims nothing
	type te_demog_trend_good_up = widget {
		size = { 24 22 }

		icon = {
			size = { 20 20 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_up.dds"
			block "trend_up" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 20 20 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_down.dds"
			block "trend_down" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 8 20 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_nochange.dds"
			block "trend_level" {}
		}
	}

	type te_demog_trend_good_down = widget {
		size = { 24 22 }

		icon = {
			size = { 20 20 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_down.dds"
			mirror = vertical
			block "trend_up" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 20 20 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_up.dds"
			mirror = vertical
			block "trend_down" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 8 20 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_nochange.dds"
			block "trend_level" {}
		}
	}

	type te_demog_trend_neutral = widget {
		size = { 24 22 }

		icon = {
			size = { 18 8 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/politics_view/summary_arrow_down.dds"
			mirror = vertical
			block "trend_up" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 18 8 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/politics_view/summary_arrow_down.dds"
			block "trend_down" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 8 20 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/trend_nochange.dds"
			block "trend_level" {}
		}
	}

	### One five-year band of the pyramid: the men's bar growing left from the
	### centre, the band's ages, the women's bar growing right. Fixed cells,
	### 196 + 64 + 196 and two 12 px gaps = 480.
	###
	### Each bar is two layers in one 196 x 14 cell. Behind, full height and
	### pale (the bar's own colour at 35%), the band twenty years ahead; in
	### front, 8 px high and centred, the band now. So the pale band shows
	### round the solid bar as far as the outline reaches, and past its end
	### when the band will grow: where the pale stops is the band in twenty
	### years, where the solid stops is the band today. The plain rule-5 form
	### (solid to the lower of the two, pale to the higher) would draw a
	### shrinking band's solid bar at its future size, and the pyramid's first
	### job is today's shape.
	###
	### The men's bars are vanilla's REVERSE HACK (gui/shared/progressbars.gui,
	### double_direction_progressbar's left half): progress and no-progress
	### textures swapped and a range of -max .. 0, with the value negated, so
	### the coloured part runs from the value to the right-hand end.
	###
	### Blocks: "band_label" (the ages), "men_now", "women_now", "men_next",
	### "women_next" (each a `value`), "next_visible" (the outline's gate),
	### "men_range" and "women_range" (min and max; the country's
	### te_dg_pyr_max by default, so a state's pyramid overrides them),
	### and "row_tooltip".
	type te_demog_pyramid_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 12
		block "row_tooltip" {}

		widget = {
			size = { 196 14 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			widget = {
				size = { 196 14 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				block "next_visible" {}

				progressbar = {
					size = { 196 14 }
					parentanchor = vcenter
					direction = horizontal
					progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
					noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
					texture_density = 2
					skip_initial_animation = yes
					alwaystransparent = yes
					color = { 0.36 0.56 0.82 0.35 }
					block "men_range" {
						min = "[Negate_float( FixedPointToFloat( GetPlayer.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_pyr_max').GetValue ) )]"
						max = 0
					}
					block "men_next" {}
				}
			}
			progressbar = {
				size = { 196 8 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				direction = horizontal
				progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
				noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
				texture_density = 2
				skip_initial_animation = yes
				alwaystransparent = yes
				color = { 0.36 0.56 0.82 1.0 }
				block "men_range" {
					min = "[Negate_float( FixedPointToFloat( GetPlayer.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_pyr_max').GetValue ) )]"
					max = 0
				}
				block "men_now" {}
			}
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 64 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 64 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			block "band_label" {}
		}

		widget = {
			size = { 196 14 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			widget = {
				size = { 196 14 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				block "next_visible" {}

				progressbar = {
					size = { 196 14 }
					parentanchor = vcenter
					direction = horizontal
					progresstexture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
					noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
					texture_density = 2
					skip_initial_animation = yes
					alwaystransparent = yes
					color = { 0.82 0.42 0.44 0.35 }
					block "women_range" {
						min = 0
						max = "[FixedPointToFloat( GetPlayer.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_pyr_max').GetValue )]"
					}
					block "women_next" {}
				}
			}
			progressbar = {
				size = { 196 8 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				direction = horizontal
				progresstexture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
				noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
				texture_density = 2
				skip_initial_animation = yes
				alwaystransparent = yes
				color = { 0.82 0.42 0.44 1.0 }
				block "women_range" {
					min = 0
					max = "[FixedPointToFloat( GetPlayer.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_pyr_max').GetValue )]"
				}
				block "women_now" {}
			}
		}
	}

	### One term of Wealth Concentration's target as a pillar (the Colonial
	### Empire's colonial_empire_pillar_row): its name, a bar either side of a
	### centre line on one shared scale of -50 .. +50, so the terms compare,
	### and its signed value. Fixed cells, 190 + 190 + 72, two 8 px gaps and
	### the 4 px margins = 476.
	###
	### The bar is drawn here rather than with vanilla's double bar, whose
	### halves are red and green: neither direction is good or bad for the
	### player in itself (rule 5), so both halves take one neutral fill. The
	### left half is the reverse hack, as the pyramid's men's bars are. Blocks:
	### "term_left" (the value, clamped to 0 or below) and "term_right" (0 or
	### above).
	type te_demog_term_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 8
		margin = { 4 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 190 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 190 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 190 14 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			icon = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
				color = { 0.50 0.50 0.50 0.20 }
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 95 14 }
				parentanchor = left|vcenter

				progressbar = {
					size = { 95 14 }
					direction = horizontal
					progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
					noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
					texture_density = 2
					skip_initial_animation = yes
					alwaystransparent = yes
					color = { 0.78 0.68 0.46 1.0 }
					min = -50
					max = 0
					block "term_left" {}
				}
			}
			widget = {
				size = { 95 14 }
				parentanchor = right|vcenter

				progressbar = {
					size = { 95 14 }
					direction = horizontal
					progresstexture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
					noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
					texture_density = 2
					skip_initial_animation = yes
					alwaystransparent = yes
					color = { 0.78 0.68 0.46 1.0 }
					min = 0
					max = 50
					block "term_right" {}
				}
			}
			icon = {
				size = { 2 18 }
				parentanchor = center
				texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
				color = { 0.96 0.90 0.72 0.80 }
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 72 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 72 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#v"
			elide = right
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### The States table's column heads, each with its hover. Fixed cells as te_demog_state_row's, past its 4 px inset.
	type te_demog_state_head = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		margin_left = 4

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 146 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 146 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_states_head_state"
			tooltip = "te_demog_states_head_state_tt"
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 60 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 60 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_states_head_people"
			tooltip = "te_demog_states_head_people_tt"
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 56 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 56 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_states_head_e0"
			tooltip = "te_demog_states_head_e0_tt"
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 60 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 60 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_states_head_median"
			tooltip = "te_demog_states_head_median_tt"
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 76 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 76 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_states_head_tfr"
			tooltip = "te_demog_states_head_tfr_tt"
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 56 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 56 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_states_head_gini"
			tooltip = "te_demog_states_head_gini_tt"
		}
	}

	### One state of te_dg_states or te_dg_states_top (datacontext State), a button that opens the state on its
	### Demographics subtab: OpenStatePanel, then the Population tab's subtab flag, two onclicks in order as vanilla's
	### building browser chains its filters; which state-panel tab opens is a play-test check. Hovering highlights the
	### state on the map, a right click opens its menu, as the Budget panel's state rows do. Fixed cells, 4 + 146 + 60 +
	### 56 + 60 + 76 + 56 and five 4 px gaps = 478. The state's name shrinks to 12 before it would elide ("South
	### Atlantic Islands", 22 characters, is about 145 at 12; the guide's rule 3, option 4, for a name read to find a
	### row): every other cell holds its longest figure at 17. The tooltip reads only State (gotcha #24): the sex balance
	### and Wealth Concentration the table's columns gave up.
	type te_demog_state_row = button {
		using = default_button
		size = { 480 28 }
		tooltip = "te_demog_state_row_tt"
		onclick = "[InformationPanelBar.OpenStatePanel( State.AccessSelf )]"
		onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set('population_subtab', 'te_demog')]"
		onrightclick = "[RightClickMenuManager.ShowForState(State.AccessSelf)]"
		onmousehierarchyenter = "[AccessHighlightManager.HighlightState(State.Self)]"
		onmousehierarchyleave = "[AccessHighlightManager.RemoveHighlight]"

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 4
			position = { 4 0 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				minimumsize = { 146 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 146 -1 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = te_demog_fontsize_row
				fontsize_min = 12
				elide = right
				text = "[State.GetNameNoFormatting]"
			}
			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				minimumsize = { 60 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 60 -1 }
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = te_demog_fontsize_row
				default_format = "#v"
				text = "[State.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_people').GetValue|K]"
			}
			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				minimumsize = { 56 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 56 -1 }
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = te_demog_fontsize_row
				default_format = "#v"
				text = "[State.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_e0').GetValue|1]"
			}
			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				minimumsize = { 60 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 60 -1 }
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = te_demog_fontsize_row
				default_format = "#v"
				text = "[State.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_median').GetValue|1]"
			}
			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				minimumsize = { 76 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 76 -1 }
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = te_demog_fontsize_row
				default_format = "#v"
				text = "[State.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_tfr').GetValue|2]"
			}
			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				minimumsize = { 56 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 56 -1 }
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = te_demog_fontsize_row
				default_format = "#v"
				text = "[State.MakeScope.Var('te_dg_gini').GetValue|2]"
			}
		}
	}

	### One of the three largest cities (te_dg_cities; datacontext State): the
	### state, which counts as one city, and its urban people. Fixed cells,
	### 300 + 176 and a 4 px gap = 480.
	type te_demog_city_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		tooltip = "te_demog_city_row_tt"

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 300 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 300 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			fontsize_min = 12
			elide = right
			text = "[State.GetNameNoFormatting]"
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 176 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 176 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			elide = right
			text = "te_demog_city_row_value"
		}
	}

	### A cell of the Wealth section's first row: a small heading over a figure.
	### 120 wide for the Gini, 112 for each stratum's income: 120 + 3 x 112 and
	### three 8 px gaps = 480.
	type te_demog_wealth_cell = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "cell_size" {
			minimumsize = { 112 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 112 -1 }
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			parentanchor = hcenter
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "cell_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			parentanchor = hcenter
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			block "cell_value" {}
		}
	}

	### A cell of the overview's grid (gui_style_guide.md rule 4; Banking's te_banking_ov_cell): a box 238 x 70 with its
	### icon in an inset box of its own down the left, and beside it three lines: the caption, the reading and a figure
	### beneath it. Two to a row, 238 + 4 + 238 = 480. The lines start at x 78 and may take 154 (238 - 78 - 6): every
	### caption, reading and third line is held to it (test_demographics_layout's WidthTest). A reading with an arrow
	### carries it over the icon box's top-right corner ("trend", a te_demog_trend_* type), where Banking's crash badge
	### sits. The instance sets the cell's tooltip (the old row's hover, rule 2), "icon" (a texture), "caption", "word"
	### and "third_line" (texts) and, where the reading has one, "trend".
	type te_demog_ov_cell = widget {
		size = { 238 70 }

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_simple
		}

		### The icon's own box, inset in the cell's: 52 square from x 6, the icon 44 inside it.
		widget = {
			size = { 52 52 }
			position = { 6 0 }
			parentanchor = left|vcenter

			background = {
				using = dark_area
				alpha = 0.3
			}

			icon = {
				size = { 44 44 }
				parentanchor = center
				block "icon" {}
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			position = { 78 2 }
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 154
			elide = right
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_overview
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "caption" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			position = { 78 24 }
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 154
			elide = right
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_overview
			block "word" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			position = { 78 46 }
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 154
			elide = right
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_overview
			block "third_line" {}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 24 22 }
			position = { 40 3 }
			block "trend" {}
		}
	}

	### One row of the overview's grid: two cells, anchored left, so a row with one cell shown keeps it in the left column.
	type te_demog_ov_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
	}

	### The Causes of Death pie (gui_style_guide.md rule 5: a share is a pie, framed with a ring; Colonial Empire's
	### te_ce_ov_pie): 104 square, the ring behind and eight stacked progresspie layers inside it, each filled to the
	### shares summed through its slice and the largest first, so slice n shows between the sums through n - 1 and n
	### (gui_modding_guide.md, "Pie charts of script-held data"). Clockwise from 12 o'clock: infection and hunger, chronic
	### illness and old age, accidents and violence, work, childbirth, added on top, killed by events, war (the codes of
	### te_dg_dc_lead; the textures are gen_ch_model_pie_textures.py's, frame 1 transparent and frame 2 the colour). The
	### instance sets "cum_1" .. "cum_7", each a value 0-1 (te_demog_dc_cum_<n>); the eighth layer is the whole disc.
	### Hover is per widget rectangle, so the pie has the section's one tooltip and the legend beside it names the slices.
	type te_demog_cause_pie = widget {
		size = { 104 104 }

		icon = {
			size = { 104 104 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/round_frame_dec.dds"
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 76 76 }
			parentanchor = center

			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				value = 1
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/demographics_icons/pie_war.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "cum_7" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/demographics_icons/pie_killed.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "cum_6" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/demographics_icons/pie_on_top.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "cum_5" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/demographics_icons/pie_maternal.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "cum_4" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/demographics_icons/pie_work.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "cum_3" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/demographics_icons/pie_external.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "cum_2" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/demographics_icons/pie_chronic.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "cum_1" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/demographics_icons/pie_infection.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
		}
	}

	### The legend's column heads, each with its hover. Fixed cells as te_demog_cause_row's.
	type te_demog_cause_head = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		widget = {
			size = { 14 4 }
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 186 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 186 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_dc_head_cause"
			tooltip = "te_demog_dc_head_cause_tt"
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 84 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 84 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_dc_head_deaths"
			tooltip = "te_demog_dc_head_deaths_tt"
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 56 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 56 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "te_demog_dc_head_share"
			tooltip = "te_demog_dc_head_share_tt"
		}
	}

	### One slice of the pie (gui_style_guide.md rule 5, "several related figures form a table"): its swatch (the slice's
	### own texture, frame 2), its name (hover the row for its rate and what sets it, rule 2: the cause multipliers the
	### section's rows used to show), last year's deaths and their share. Fixed cells, 14 + 186 + 84 + 56 and three 4 px
	### gaps = 352, beside the 104 pie and an 8 px gap: 464. The instance sets the row's tooltip, "swatch" (a texture),
	### "cause", "deaths" and "share".
	type te_demog_cause_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		icon = {
			size = { 14 14 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			framesize = { 128 128 }
			frame = 2
			block "swatch" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 186 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 186 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			elide = right
			block "cause" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 84 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 84 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#v"
			elide = right
			block "deaths" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 56 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 56 -1 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = te_demog_fontsize_row
			default_format = "#v"
			elide = right
			block "share" {}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### ======================================================================

	### The overview, always shown and with no header (gui_style_guide.md rule 1): the country's census, its states added up, as Banking's
	### grid of icon cells, two to a row (rule 4; issue #1029). Each cell's hover is its old row's (rule 2); the
	### rows it dropped are in their sections: the sex balance in the pyramid's, old age from and youth in Work and
	### Retirement's, Living to 100 and biological age in Longevity's, the urban pattern in Where People Live.
	### Every figure is picked by its gate (a stepped census for the rates, deaths by cause for the leading cause),
	### so a figure not yet written is never read. Icons are placeholders: docs/systems/demographics_gui_icons.md.
	type te_demog_overview = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes

		te_demog_panel = {
			spacing = 4

			te_demog_text = {
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "te_demog_ov_census"
				tooltip = "te_demog_ov_census_tt"
			}
			### Natural Change and Net Migration
			te_demog_ov_row = {
				te_demog_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "te_demog_ov_nat_tt"
					blockoverride "icon" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/population.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_nat"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_stepped_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_nat_value', 'te_demog_ov_cell_pending' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "third_line" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_stepped_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_nat_third', 'te_tt_blank' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "trend" {
						te_demog_trend_neutral = {
							blockoverride "trend_up" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_natural'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
							}
							blockoverride "trend_down" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_natural'), '(CFixedPoint)-1' )]"
							}
							blockoverride "trend_level" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_natural'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
							}
						}
					}
				}
				te_demog_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "te_demog_ov_mig_cell_tt"
					blockoverride "icon" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/state_status_icons/mass_migration_target.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_mig"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_stepped_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_mig_cell_value', 'te_demog_ov_cell_pending' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "third_line" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_stepped_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_mig_third', 'te_tt_blank' )]"
					}
				}
			}
			### Life Expectancy and the Leading Cause of Death
			te_demog_ov_row = {
				te_demog_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_lx_e0_over_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_e0_tt_100', 'te_demog_ov_e0_tt' )]"
					blockoverride "icon" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/diplomatic_treaties_articles_icons/healthcare_aid.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_e0"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_lx_e0_over_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_e0_100', 'te_demog_ov_e0_value' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "third_line" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_e0_third"
					}
					blockoverride "trend" {
						te_demog_trend_good_up = {
							blockoverride "trend_up" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_e0'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
							}
							blockoverride "trend_down" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_e0'), '(CFixedPoint)-1' )]"
							}
							blockoverride "trend_level" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_e0'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
							}
						}
					}
				}
				te_demog_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_dc_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_lead_tt', 'te_demog_ov_lead_pending_tt' )]"
					blockoverride "icon" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/red_cross.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_lead"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_dc_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_lead_value', 'te_demog_ov_cell_pending' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "third_line" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_dc_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_lead_third', 'te_tt_blank' )]"
					}
				}
			}
			### Fertility and Median Age
			te_demog_ov_row = {
				te_demog_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "te_demog_ov_tfr_tt"
					blockoverride "icon" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/decree/decree_natalism_initiative.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_fert"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_fert_value"
					}
					blockoverride "third_line" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( Not( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_tfr'), '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ), 'te_demog_ov_fert_third', 'te_tt_blank' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "trend" {
						te_demog_trend_neutral = {
							blockoverride "trend_up" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_tfr'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
							}
							blockoverride "trend_down" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_tfr'), '(CFixedPoint)-1' )]"
							}
							blockoverride "trend_level" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_tfr'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
							}
						}
					}
				}
				te_demog_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "te_demog_ov_median_tt"
					blockoverride "icon" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/clock.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_median"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_median_value"
					}
					blockoverride "third_line" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_median_third"
					}
					blockoverride "trend" {
						te_demog_trend_neutral = {
							blockoverride "trend_up" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_median'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
							}
							blockoverride "trend_down" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_median'), '(CFixedPoint)-1' )]"
							}
							blockoverride "trend_level" {
								visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('te_demog_trend_median'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			### Working Age and the Gini
			te_demog_ov_row = {
				te_demog_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_work_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_working_age_tt', 'te_demog_ov_working_age_pending_tt' )]"
					blockoverride "icon" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/institution_icons/institution_ministry_of_labor.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_working_age"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_work_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_working_age_value', 'te_demog_ov_cell_pending' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "third_line" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_work_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_working_third', 'te_tt_blank' )]"
					}
				}
				te_demog_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "te_demog_ov_gini_tt"
					blockoverride "icon" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/money.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "caption" {
						text = "te_demog_ov_gini"
					}
					blockoverride "word" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_gini_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_gini_value', 'te_demog_ov_cell_pending' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "third_line" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_wealth_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_ov_gini_third', 'te_tt_blank' )]"
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### Causes of Death (issue #1029; the state subtab's since the owner's 2026-10-11 design): the country's, its states' deaths summed. First
	### last year's deaths per 1,000 people, then the pie of those deaths by cause and its legend (rule 5): the
	### census's own deaths split by an estimate over its bands (te_demog_cause_deaths_estimate), childbirth's, the
	### deaths added on top under Full, the war dead and the people killed by events as counted. Each legend row's
	### hover gives its cause's rate against a poor country's and what sets it (by people across our states, and the capital's).
	### Then Health Care Access, people-weighted. Open by default (rule 1), its own flag.
	### The pie waits for a count with deaths by cause (te_demog_dc_ready_sgui); until then one line.
	type te_demog_sec_causes = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 2

		te_demog_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "te_demog_sec_causes"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('te_demog_causes_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('te_demog_causes_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('te_demog_causes_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		te_demog_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('te_demog_causes_closed'))]"

			### Deaths per 1,000 people last year, which the pie below splits
			te_demog_figure_row = {
				tooltip = "te_demog_cd_cdr_tt"
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "te_demog_cd_cdr"
				}
				blockoverride "row_value" {
					text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_stepped_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_demog_cd_cdr_value', 'te_demog_ov_pending' )]"
				}
			}
			te_demog_text = {
				visible = "[Not( GetScriptedGui('te_demog_dc_ready_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
				text = "te_demog_cd_dc_pending"
			}
			### The pie and its legend: last year's deaths by cause
			flowcontainer = {
